# Illustrative semantic data contract for a financial statement read as a matrix
# (spec 2026-10-12-a-matrix-cell-is-an-observation-design.md § 4).
# CC-BY-4.0 — François Rosselet, 2026. Part of the ET(K)L method, https://w3id.org/iladub/etkl.
# Synthetic: the line items are generic statement lines and no figure of any issuer appears.
#
# THREE FIELDS, ONE PER STRUCTURAL ROLE. A statement prints one figure per (line, period): the
# row label says which line, the column header path says which period, the cell is the figure.
# So the contract declares what each POSITION means, with `etkl:fieldRole`, and no field is
# found by matching a label to a field name. That is what turns the per-cell reading on:
# `feed.ground_document` reads one record per cell exactly when a field declares `etkl:CellValue`.
#
# EACH FIELD HAS ITS OWN ORACLE, and the role is none of them. The role picks the field; what may
# ground is decided by the field's scheme (`lineItem`) or by its value constraint in
# statement-shapes.ttl (`period`, `value`).
#
# WHAT IS NOT DECLARED, and why (spec § 6): no measure name and no unit. A statement's heading
# may say "in millions, except per-share amounts", so no one unit is true of every cell; the
# figure is carried as printed and the line item says what it measures. No period is normalised
# either: the period is the text the column header prints.
@prefix fin:  <https://example.org/finance#> .
@prefix etkl: <https://w3id.org/iladub/etkl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

fin:statement-contract a etkl:SemanticDataContract ;
    rdfs:label "Statement figure, by line item and period"@en ;
    etkl:targetClass fin:StatementFigure ;
    etkl:requiresKnowledge fin:scheme-line-item ;
    etkl:hasField fin:f-line-item , fin:f-period , fin:f-value .

fin:f-line-item a etkl:Field ; etkl:fillsProperty fin:lineItem ; etkl:fieldRole etkl:RowKey ;
    etkl:admissibleScheme fin:scheme-line-item .
fin:f-period    a etkl:Field ; etkl:fillsProperty fin:period ;   etkl:fieldRole etkl:ColumnKey .
fin:f-value     a etkl:Field ; etkl:fillsProperty fin:value ;    etkl:fieldRole etkl:CellValue .
